 "prompt": "Create a deck for Parcelbird's board: Should Parcelbird launch its own quick-commerce grocery delivery service in 2027?\n\nThe briefing pack in ./evidence/briefing-pack.md has everything that is available: work only from it. Web research is not available.\n\nSave the finished deliverable in ./deliverable/.\n\nI won't be available to answer questions while you work. Wherever you would ask me something, choose the option you would recommend, note your choice, and carry on until the deliverable is finished.\n\nHow to approach it:\n- Work hypothesis-driven. State an initial answer early, write down what would have to be true for it to hold, test each of those against the evidence, and change the answer if the evidence does not support it.\n- Build the storyline with the pyramid principle: one governing thought that answers the question, an executive summary up front whose points become the sections, and the supporting arguments and evidence beneath each point.\n- Keep every grouping MECE (mutually exclusive, collectively exhaustive).\n- Give every slide an action title: a full-sentence takeaway that the slide's content proves.\n- Base the recommendation on evidence. Quantify where the data allows and show the calculations, weigh the alternatives and their trade-offs, and state the key assumptions, risks and uncertainties.",
